From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Topher Campbell <chrs2021@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 03/16] pmdomain: mediatek: mt8183: keep CONN on through system suspend

The connectivity subsystem keeps running while the AP sleeps (its
firmware, the Wi-Fi association). With MTK_SCPD_ACTIVE_WAKEUP the CONN
domain stays on for a device in the wakeup path; the MT6771's consys
driver marks itself so. Without it genpd switched CONN off in
suspend_noirq and Wi-Fi was dead after resume.
---
 drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mt8183-pm-domains.h | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mt8183-pm-domains.h b/drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mt8183-pm-domains.h
index c4c1b63d85b1943aafdb295d21026835ddc74ff3..0c16b4f2c7062b133c423015123902f55e7d6170 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mt8183-pm-domains.h
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mt8183-pm-domains.h
@@ -28,6 +28,8 @@ static const struct scpsys_domain_data scpsys_domain_data_mt8183[] = {
 		.pwr_sta2nd_offs = 0x0184,
 		.sram_pdn_bits = 0,
 		.sram_pdn_ack_bits = 0,
+		/* CONNSYS runs on through system suspend (MT6771's consys driver) */
+		.caps = MTK_SCPD_ACTIVE_WAKEUP,
 		.bp_cfg = {
 			BUS_PROT_WR(INFRA,
 				    MT8183_TOP_AXI_PROT_EN_CONN,
